            {
                "entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
                "word": "inaliénable",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6dd190c4-34dc-4cfd-840e-ef511c542266",
                        "entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "inaliénables"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "be6cd68a-b88e-3241-86ca-5e683c59ff94",
                        "entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui ne peut s’aliéner. Qui ne peut être enlevé."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6022b191-3c34-486c-bbb4-71b4942d1571",
                                "sense_id": "be6cd68a-b88e-3241-86ca-5e683c59ff94",
                                "text": "Les Représentants du Peuple Français … ont résolu d'exposer, dans une Déclaration solennelle, les droits naturels, inaliénables et sacrés de l'Homme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf321d24-d6f9-48f1-9f5b-3eed2fc3857b",
                                "sense_id": "be6cd68a-b88e-3241-86ca-5e683c59ff94",
                                "text": "Laissons donc les grands propriétaires anglais avec leurs immenses fortunes et leurs immenses propriétés inaliénables, faire des choses qu’il est impossible de mettre en pratique chez nous."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2fb84145-1b3e-384d-876e-ce467fbeaf4f",
                        "entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une possession grammaticale dans laquelle le possédé est inséparablement lié au possesseur, le possédé étant le plus souvent une partie du corps ou un lien de parenté. Dans certaines langues, le nom inaliénable doit avoir toujours un affixe exprimant le possesseur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2ab7b87-c399-4e1d-adb7-4f21b3ae9152",
                                "sense_id": "2fb84145-1b3e-384d-876e-ce467fbeaf4f",
                                "text": "En koyukon, entseyh (nez) est un nom inaliénable ne pouvant se rencontrer isolément. On trouvera par exemple bentseyh (be + entseyh) pour dire mon nez."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19054e78-9537-432a-9b6f-f54fee113515",
                                "sense_id": "2fb84145-1b3e-384d-876e-ce467fbeaf4f",
                                "text": "On sait que les structures grammaticales qui traduisent une relation intrinsèque de possession inaliénable de manière distinctes ne sont pas universelles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23f83ce7-25b7-4388-be67-ac4a2fd93cfb",
                        "source_entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
                        "target_lang_word": "unveräußerlich",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unveräußerlich",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6995bc7e-f741-3f98-bdd6-5c2d59f0bbe9",
                                        "entry_id": "58929c10-30ad-3339-a786-b6372dc6d98b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "so, dass es nicht beseitigt/aberkannt werden darf/kann"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5de3f9c2-87a7-4c46-807c-83d745da22fb",
                                                "sense_id": "6995bc7e-f741-3f98-bdd6-5c2d59f0bbe9",
                                                "text": "„Europa steht für ein Modell, in dem Staaten und Völker sprachliche, kulturelle, ökonomische und geographische Grenzen überwinden; in dem sie ihre Wirtschaft und ihre Politik so vereinen, dass sie sich gegenseitig stärken und die Kraft, die sie dadurch erwerben, nutzen, um dem einzelnen Menschen seine unveräußerlichen Grundrechte zu garantieren.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4ecbd15-7275-3fcf-b212-dc3d74262243",
                                        "entry_id": "58929c10-30ad-3339-a786-b6372dc6d98b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "nicht zum Verkauf stehend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "253299c6-f007-42ff-856d-42d1556e49a6",
                                                "sense_id": "c4ecbd15-7275-3fcf-b212-dc3d74262243",
                                                "text": "Tut mir leid, aber dieser Oldtimer ist unveräußerlich, er ist nämlich ein Erbstück, an dem ich hänge."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d5e2538a-cdce-4543-b04c-cab2bb1d5d12",
                        "source_entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
                        "target_lang_word": "inalienable",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inalienable",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a718089-81cd-3ca6-b391-e1d1ba0db9a2",
                                        "entry_id": "42bb4c8d-45fa-3aa2-8dc9-e74cf90bf568",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not subject to being alienated, that is, surrendered, taken away, or transferred to another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de95f79e-6982-4a1c-90a2-c65d788d9dba",
                                                "sense_id": "9a718089-81cd-3ca6-b391-e1d1ba0db9a2",
                                                "text": "Near-synonyms: indelible, unsurrenderable, permanent"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eca73788-38df-49ef-9b2f-d895e1360458",
                                                "sense_id": "9a718089-81cd-3ca6-b391-e1d1ba0db9a2",
                                                "text": "An inalienable right is a right that cannot be given away nor taken away."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ddf8bf3-7bf2-46d0-81bf-06abf71ebd84",
                                                "sense_id": "9a718089-81cd-3ca6-b391-e1d1ba0db9a2",
                                                "text": "\"Know thy own worth, and reverence the lyre,\" is a line that should be as a fillet bound round the brow—a philactory embroidered on the garments of every son and daughter of Adam distinguished by the possession of that sacred gift, which, whether used or abused, applauded in itself or derided in its possessor, is the highest and the most inalienable distinction humanity ever has or ever can be gifted with, whether bestowed on the highest or the humblest being, in the great mass to which we all belong."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "424de0e2-c471-3641-ad14-6ec29efabd89",
                                        "entry_id": "42bb4c8d-45fa-3aa2-8dc9-e74cf90bf568",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or pertaining to a noun belonging to a special class in which the possessive construction differs from the norm, especially for particular familial relationships and body parts, regarding permanence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50c9793e-7dbf-4d0b-a585-510bb2226367",
                                                "sense_id": "424de0e2-c471-3641-ad14-6ec29efabd89",
                                                "text": "Just as some languages have a \"be\" for permanent states (which are essential) and a different \"be\" for temporary states (which are incidental), some languages have a \"have\" for unchangeable possession (which is inalienable) and a different \"have\" for changeable possession (which is alienable)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae598cb7-56bc-465d-95af-59fc763d2560",
                        "source_entry_id": "62ad35ff-ac24-3ee0-8187-8f727d64895c",
